"If after Vanya's move the integer is divisible by 3, then he wins."
This means Vanya wins if he can make the number $x$ such that $x \equiv 0 \pmod 3$.
Since Vanya moves first, he changes $n$ to $n \pm 1$.
If $n \pm 1 \equiv 0 \pmod 3$, Vanya wins immediately.
This happens if $n \equiv 2 \pmod 3$ (since $n+1 \equiv 0$) or $n \equiv 1 \pmod 3$ (since $n-1 \equiv 0$).
So if $n \not\equiv 0 \pmod 3$, Vanya can win on the first move.
